    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n82031" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιρραίνω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>besprinkle</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Lap.</u>
				13
			</span></i> ; esp. in sacred rites, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μιᾶς ἐκ
				χέρνιβος βωμοὺς π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				1130
			</span></i> :—
				Med.
			, <i>purify oneself</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδατι
				περίρραν᾽</span> (i.e. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περίρραναι</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				530.23
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Lyc.</u>
				2
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ συνουσίας περιραναμένους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12(1).789.15
				</span></i>
			 (Rhodes, <span class="entity">ii A. D.</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				982.8
			</span></i> (Pergam., <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span> in form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ρασάμενοι</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> π. ἀπὸ ἱεροῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Char.</u>
					16.2
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ θαλάττης</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				13
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ [κρήνης]</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristobul.
					6
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐλοχύταις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nonn.
					<u>D.</u>
					5.7
				</span></i>
			 (
				Pass.
			), etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			generally, <i>moisten</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδασι . .
